    closing: {
        heading: '9. Summary review',
        body: [
            "**Export-led.** **Marksans Pharma: own.** The one exporter with its own route to the customer, net cash and a price that fits. **Caplin Point Labs: follow.** The steadiest margins in the sector; buy when the price allows. **Rubicon Research: follow.** The best research engine, priced for it. **Granules India: wait** for one inspection. **Natco Pharma: wait** to see what the rights money buys. **Strides Pharma: wait** on the FDA, the drug quota and its pledge. **Sai Parenterals: pass** until the plants run and the margin reaches guidance.",
            "**India branded.** **Emcure Pharma: follow**, moved down from own; a great partner moat with lower-quality growth. **Corona Remedies: follow.** The cleanest business, at the highest price. **RPG Life Sciences: wait**, moved down from follow, until the API deals prove themselves. **Jagsonpal Pharma: wait** for reported growth to catch secondary sales. **Eris Lifesciences: wait** for the refinancing and the Swiss re-inspection. **Sanofi India: pass.** A dividend stream on a shrinking base. **Indoco Remedies: pass** until Goa clears and debt falls.",
            "**Hybrids.** **Zydus Lifesciences: follow**, moved down from own: a widening franchise whose FY27 profit is falling while its price is at a high. **Ipca Laboratories: wait** and **Ajanta Pharma: wait**, good companies at full prices, Ajanta with governance items to clear. **Alembic Pharma: wait** for India and the end of its exclusive launch.",
            "**Specialists.** **Sakar Healthcare: wait**, moved down from follow, for sales to catch up with its plant. **Gufic Biosciences: wait** for its EU certificate. **Wockhardt: wait** for US prescriptions and the size of its share issue. **Fredun Pharma: pass** until cash arrives. **Beta Drugs: pass**, moved down from wait, until its rating review and exports are back on track. **Orchid Pharma: avoid.** **JB Chem & Pharma** has merged into Torrent Pharma and is no longer covered.",
            "**What would change my view.** For the better: a Saroglitazar approval on time (Zydus); a clean Gagillapur or Goa re-inspection (Granules, Indoco); tariffs on generics formally ruled out in the April 2027 review (Rubicon, Strides, Marksans); Eris refinancing cleanly. For the worse: US tariffs on generics; a price-control listing for a main brand; a large, expensive acquisition by Natco or Marksans; a tax demand at Ajanta.",
            "**What to watch next quarter.** Marksans: margin and the next deal. Zydus: margin through the Saroglitazar spend, and cash. Caplin: receivables. Emcure: organic India. Corona: gross margin. Granules and Indoco: the FDA. Eris: the December bonds. Natco: the rights issue. Sakar and Beta: exports. Sai: margin and Adelaide.",
        ],
        bottomLine:
            "Separate the books, check what is inside the profit, and read the annual reports. Own Marksans Pharma; follow Zydus Lifesciences, Caplin Point Labs, Emcure Pharma, Rubicon Research and Corona Remedies for a better price; wait on Ipca, Ajanta and the event-driven names; and do not pay specialist prices for plans that keep slipping.",
    },

